  \subtree{
    \title{Runtime analysis of the Euclidean Algorithm}

    \p{In [[00JW]], you learned that the Euclidean Algorithm seems much more efficient than factoring; but how efficient is it, exactly? The problems in this section will walk you through a classic analysis of how long the Euclidean Algorithm takes to run on given inputs.  However, the problems are independent; it is possible to do each problem without having done the previous ones.}

    \p{Throughout this section, when referring to the Euclidean
    Algorithm, we will specifically work with the [recursive
    implementation](00F9) (\tt{GCDRecA} from the POGIL activity).
    }

